# Frontend build tooling — never commit installed deps or an npmrc that could pin
# a private registry URL. The BUILT output (../internal/webui/dist) IS committed so
# the Go binary embeds it and `go build`/`install.sh` need no npm.
#
# package-lock.json IS committed (generated against the PUBLIC npm registry
# https://registry.npmjs.org) so CI runs a reproducible `npm ci` + build and verifies
# the embedded dist matches source (DESIGN §CI / §0 D10). This repo-specific choice
# overrides the general "don't commit lockfiles" convention; the .npmrc stays ignored
# so no private-registry pin can leak in.
node_modules/
.npmrc
npm-shrinkwrap.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
*.tsbuildinfo
